                                               rdfs:label "transport model"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "There are several (constitutive) equations which describe the transport of matter, or properties of it, in an almost identical way. In every case, in words they read: Flux (density) is proportional to a gradient, where the constant of proportionality is a characteristic of the material. In general, the constant must be replaced by a 2nd rank tensor, to account for directional dependencies of the material."@en ;
