###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6684650
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6684650> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534292> ;
                                               rdfs:label "free flow coupled to porous media flow"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "Systems where free flow interacts with permeable media are important in many areas. Examples include soil water evaporation in environmental science, exchange between blood vessels in medicine or water management in fuel cells. To understand these processes, it is necessary to capture the interaction between the two flow regions. In this specific case we consider a stationary, single-phase flow where creeping Stokes flow describes the free-flow region and Darcy’s law governs the porous medium."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534269> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1513> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6675408> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1640> :File:FreeFlowPorousDomain.png ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P286> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6376356> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "coupled systems of free flow of an incompressible fluid adjacent to permeable media"@en .


