                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "The Freundlich isotherm model is an empirical adsorption model that describes how solutes adhere to heterogeneous surfaces with varying affinities. It accounts for multilayer adsorption rather than a single uniform layer. The model is widely applied in environmental and chemical engineering to study pollutant adsorption on materials such as activated carbon, soil, and biochar."@en ;
