                                               rdfs:label "linear parameter estimation (Flory-Huggins model)"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This task uses the linearized Flory–Huggins equation to estimate the equilibrium constant and occupation number from transformed equilibrium data. Linear regression provides a straightforward estimation method, but may introduce bias due to logarithmic transformation. The resulting parameters characterize adsorption feasibility and the extent of surface site occupation in the Flory–Huggins model."@en ;
