###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821119
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821119> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
                                               rdfs:label "nonlinear parameter estimation (Redlich-Peterson model)"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This task performs nonlinear parameter estimation using experimental adsorption equilibrium data. The objective is to determine the Redlich-Peterson constant, coefficient, and exponent by directly fitting the nonlinear Redlich-Peterson equation to measured solute concentration and adsorbed amount data. Nonlinear regression preserves the full hybrid functional form, allowing the model to transition smoothly between Langmuir-like and Freundlich-like behavior. The resulting parameters quantify adsorption affinity, heterogeneity, and the degree of deviation from ideal monolayer adsorption."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1560> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775715> ,
