###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821281
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821281> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "intercepted photosynthetically active radiation"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "Intercepted photosynthetically active radiation represents the portion of incoming solar radiation that is absorbed by the crop canopy and available for photosynthesis. It is computed as a function of total solar radiation and canopy leaf area. This quantity determines the energy input for potential biomass growth. It is a central driver of radiation-based crop growth models."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "radiation intercepted by the crop canopy"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821282
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821282> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "canopy light attenuation coefficient"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This coefficient quantifies the exponential attenuation of incoming radiation as it passes through a plant canopy. It represents the combined effects of absorption and scattering by leaves and other plant organs. The parameter is used in Beer–Lambert type equations to estimate radiation interception from leaf area index. Its value depends on canopy architecture and leaf orientation. It is a specialization of a general attenuation coefficient applied to plant canopies."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "attenuation of light within a plant canopy"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821283
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821283> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "photosynthetically active solar radiation fraction"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "solar radiation conversion fraction"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821284
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821284> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "potential biomass increment"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the increase in crop dry matter biomass during a single day under optimal conditions. It is computed from intercepted photosynthetically active radiation and a crop-specific conversion efficiency. The value reflects the maximum attainable biomass growth for that day. It contributes to the accumulation of total potential crop biomass over the growing season."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "potential daily increase in crop biomass"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821285
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821285> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "radiation use efficiency parameter"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This crop-specific parameter defines the efficiency with which intercepted photosynthetically active radiation is converted into dry matter biomass. It represents physiological and biochemical characteristics of the crop. Higher values indicate more efficient biomass production per unit of absorbed radiation. The parameter is assumed constant under optimal growth conditions."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "converts radiation into biomass"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821286
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821286> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "change in daylength"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the daily change in daylength relative to the previous day. It accounts for seasonal variation in photoperiod. It modifies the radiation-driven biomass production term. The quantity introduces a temporal adjustment to potential growth."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "daily change in daylight duration"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821287
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821287> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "daylength"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "Daylength represents the number of hours between sunrise and sunset for a given day and location. It depends on Earth’s axial tilt and orbital position relative to the Sun."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "daylight duration"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821288
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821288> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "solar declination angle"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "The solar declination angle describes the angular position of the Sun relative to Earth’s equatorial plane. It varies predictably throughout the year due to Earth’s axial tilt. This angle determines the apparent height of the Sun and the length of daylight at a given latitude. It is a standard astronomical variable used in photoperiod calculations."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "angle between Sun and equatorial plane"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821289
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821289> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "day index"@en ;
