###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821297
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821297> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "heat unit factor"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "The heat unit factor expresses the relative progress of crop development on a normalized scale from zero to one. It is derived from the accumulated heat unit index using a crop-specific sigmoid function. HUF is used to regulate phenology-dependent growth processes. It provides a smooth, continuous representation of crop development stage."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "normalized crop development factor"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821298
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821298> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "heat unit response shape parameters"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "These crop-specific parameters determine the shape and steepness of the sigmoid relationship between heat unit index and heat unit factor. They are computed by fitting the heat unit factor equation to two predefined calibration points. The parameters remain constant throughout the simulation. They reflect phenological characteristics specific to each crop."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "shape parameters of HUF sigmoid curve"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821299
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821299> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "accumulated potential biomass"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the cumulative dry matter biomass produced by a crop under potential growth conditions. It is obtained by summing daily potential biomass increments over time. The value reflects the maximum attainable biomass prior to stress reduction and partitioning. It serves as the basis for modeling structural development and yield formation."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "total potential crop dry matter"@en .


