###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821349
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821349> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
                                               rdfs:label "nonlinear parameter estimation (Baudu model)"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This task performs nonlinear parameter estimation using adsorption equilibrium data to fit the Baudu isotherm model. The objective is to estimate the reference monolayer capacity, reference affinity constant, and the two empirical exponents describing their concentration dependence. The nonlinear fitting approach preserves the intrinsic structure of the Baudu equation and avoids bias introduced by linearization. The resulting parameters quantify surface heterogeneity and explain deviations from constant Langmuir behavior over wide concentration ranges."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1560> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775715> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775716> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821338> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821339> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821340> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821341> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821343> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821344> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821345> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1684> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775714> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "nonlinear estimation of Baudu isotherm parameters"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821350
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821350> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
                                               rdfs:label "Baudu isotherm model"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "The Baudu isotherm model is an empirical adsorption model derived from the Langmuir equation by allowing both the adsorption affinity and the monolayer capacity to vary with equilibrium concentration. It was introduced to account for systematic deviations from constant Langmuir parameters observed over wide concentration ranges. By expressing the Langmuir constants as power-law functions of concentration, the model captures surface heterogeneity and concentration-dependent adsorption behavior. At low surface coverage, the Baudu model reduces to the Freundlich isotherm, while retaining a monolayer adsorption structure. The model has been reported to provide improved fits compared with other four-parameter monolayer isotherms in liquid-phase adsorption systems."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P147> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821349> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1560> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821343> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821344> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821345> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821346> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821347> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1684> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775713> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P286> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775858> ,
                                                                                          <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821348> ,
                                                                                          <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821374> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "empirical four-parameter monolayer adsorption isotherm"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821351
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821351> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
                                               rdfs:label "computation of daylength"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This task computes the duration of daylight for a given day and geographic location using latitude and solar declination angle. The task produces a deterministic estimate of photoperiod for each simulation day. The resulting daylength is used to modulate radiation-driven and phenology-dependent biological processes."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1560> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6480497> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821287> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821289> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821302> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821303> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "calculates daily daylight duration"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821352
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821352> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
                                               rdfs:label "daylength model"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This model estimates the duration of daylight for a given day and geographic location using astronomical relationships between the Earth and the Sun. Daylength is calculated from latitude and the seasonal variation of the Sun’s declination angle, which arises from Earth’s axial tilt and orbital motion. The model provides a deterministic and time-dependent representation of photoperiod that varies systematically over the year. It does not include biological or atmospheric processes and relies solely on geometric principles. The resulting daylength is used as an environmental forcing variable in crop growth and phenological models."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P147> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821351> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1560> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821302> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821303> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P286> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821276> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "astronomical model to estimate the daylength"@en .


