###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821375
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821375> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
                                               rdfs:label "nonlinear parameter estimation (Weber-van Vliet model)"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This task performs nonlinear parameter estimation using experimental adsorption equilibrium data. The objective is to determine the Weber-van Vliet model parameters by fitting the nonlinear Weber-van Vliet equation to measured equilibrium solute concentration and adsorbed amount data. The fitting procedure minimizes deviations between experimental observations and model predictions across the full concentration range. The resulting parameters provide a flexible empirical representation of adsorption behavior when simpler isotherm models are inadequate. The task is commonly applied in adsorption studies related to chemical wastewater treatment."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1560> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775715> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775716> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821366> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821367> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821368> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821369> ,
                                                                                           <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821372> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P558> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q4115075> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "nonlinear estimation of Weber-van Vliet parameters"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821376
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821376> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
                                               rdfs:label "Weber-van Vliet isotherm model"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "The Weber-van Vliet isotherm model is an empirical adsorption model developed to describe equilibrium adsorption behavior using a flexible four-parameter formulation. It directly relates equilibrium solute concentration to adsorbed amount without assuming ideal monolayer adsorption or a specific adsorption mechanism. The model is particularly useful when classical two-parameter isotherms such as Langmuir or Freundlich fail to fit experimental data over wide concentration ranges. Due to its empirical nature, the parameters do not have a strict physical interpretation but provide high flexibility in curve fitting. The model has been applied in adsorption studies relevant to chemical and environmental engineering, including wastewater treatment."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P147> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821375> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1560> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821372> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P286> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775724> ,
                                                                                          <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775858> ,
                                                                                          <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821373> ,
                                                                                          <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821374> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "empirical four-parameter adsorption isotherm model"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821377
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821377> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "total root weight increment"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the potential daily increase in crop root biomass on a specific day. It is computed as the portion of total biomass growth allocated to the root system. The value reflects phenology-dependent carbon partitioning rather than independent root growth. It is used to update the total root biomass and to drive subsequent root distribution calculations. It is expressed as a mass per unit area."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "daily change in total root weight"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821378
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821378> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "root weight in soil layer increment"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the root weight increment allocated to a specific soil layer. It is a portion of the total root weight increment."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "daily change in root weight in soil layer"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821379
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821379> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "plant water use rate in soil layer"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the amount of water extracted by plant roots from a specific soil layer on a specific day. It reflects both root presence and soil water availability in that layer. Water use is reduced when soil moisture is limiting or when root stress factors restrict root function."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "plant water use rate in soil layer considering soil moisture"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821380
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821380> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "rooting depth"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the vertical extent of the crop root system on a specific day. It defines the maximum soil depth from which roots can extract water and nutrients. Rooting depth increases as the crop develops and is capped by the soil profile depth. The value constrains root biomass distribution and soil–plant exchange processes. It is expressed as a length."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1684> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821381> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "depth of roots"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821381
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821381> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "maximum root depth"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the maximum rooting depth attainable by a crop under ideal soil conditions. It is a crop-specific parameter reflecting genetic potential for root system expansion."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "crop-specific maximum rooting depth under ideal soil conditions"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821382
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821382> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
                                               rdfs:label "root zone depth"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This quantity represents the depth of the soil profile available for root growth. It constrains the maximum rooting depth that can be attained regardless of crop potential. It reflects physical soil limitations such as bedrock or impermeable layers."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "maximum depth available for root growth in the soil profile"@en .


###  https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821383
<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821383> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P983> "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ,
                                                                                          "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>T</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ,
                                                                                          "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>Δ</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P989> "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mi>Δ</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ;
                                               rdfs:label "root biomass partitioning equation"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This equation computes the potential daily increase in root biomass by allocating a fraction of total crop biomass growth to the root system. The allocation fraction decreases linearly with phenological development, reflecting empirical observations that crops invest more biomass in roots during early growth stages than at maturity. At emergence, a larger share of biomass is assigned to root growth, while this share is reduced as the crop develops. The formulation represents a simplified biomass partitioning rule rather than an independent root growth process. The resulting root biomass increment is used as input for subsequent root distribution and soil interaction calculations."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "computes fraction of biomass allocated to roots"@en .

