                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P989> "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ;
                                               rdfs:label "optimal plant nitrogen concentration equation"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This equation describes the decline of optimal plant nitrogen concentration with crop development stage. The concentration is modeled as a nonlinear function of the heat unit index using crop-specific parameters. It reflects the physiological tendency of plants to have high nitrogen concentrations during early growth and lower concentrations near maturity. The formulation provides a smooth, development-dependent target nitrogen concentration for demand estimation."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "estimates ideal crop nitrogen concentration as function of development"@en .

