                                                                                          "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>i</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ,
                                                                                          "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>l</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P989> "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math>"@en ;
                                               rdfs:label "adjusted nitrogen uptake equation"@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1459> "This equation scales the layer-specific nitrogen supply to ensure consistency with total crop nitrogen demand. When mass flow supply exceeds demand, uptake is reduced proportionally across layers; when supply is insufficient, the formulation allows increased uptake, representing diffusion-driven compensation. An upper constraint ensures that uptake from a layer cannot exceed the available nitrate in that layer. The equation produces the actual nitrogen uptake used by the crop model."@en ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1460> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696> ;
                                               <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P1495> <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265> ;
                                               <https://schema.org/description> "adjusts soil nitrogen supply to crop nitrogen demand"@en .

